cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "Please cite the specific version of this work that you use."
type: article
title: "Valuation balance and local lifting for cyclic n-roots"
authors:
  - family-names: Kline
    given-names: Jeff
version: 0.1.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/jeff-kline/cyclic-n-roots-valuation-balance"
license: GPL-3.0-only
keywords:
  - cyclic n-roots
  - Björck-Saffari conjecture
  - discrete Fourier transform
  - Puiseux series
  - complex Hadamard matrices
abstract: >-
  Along any Laurent-series solution of the Fourier form of the cyclic n-root
  equations, the multiset of coordinate valuations equals the multiset of
  valuations of the Fourier transform; this is a consequence of a known
  residue principle for master functions, and no priority is claimed for it. It gives exact complementary supports of
  equal size in time and frequency at every proper valuation gap. For a one-dimensional endpoint
  kernel and a nondegenerate normal critical point, local lifting reduces to
  one analytic function whose first two conditions are explicit scalars
  kappa = 0 and mu = 0. At order 26 one support pair has boundary points with
  kappa nonzero and at least two where an affine reflection forces kappa = 0
  exactly; at two of these a rigorous pi-adic computation gives mu nonzero, so
  no branch leaves them in the prescribed directions. No finiteness theorem
  for a composite order is proved; the number of coefficient conditions needed
  in general and branches in other directions are left open. Novelty is not
  established.
